Sure! To change the label of a `break` node to `'loopEnd'`, you just need to pass the node (in string form) and the new label to the `updateBreak` function. Here’s how you’d do it:

```javascript
const result = await functions.updateBreak({
  node: /* your break node as a JSON string */,
  label: 'loopEnd'
});
```

If the node already has the label `'loopEnd'`, the function will leave it unchanged. Just replace the comment with your actual node data and run it. Let me know if you need help formatting the node or anything else!
